<title>FRANCE: Air France to examine AOM buy - report.</title>
<headline>Air France to examine AOM buy - report.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air France and its shareholders will study the possibility of buying AOM airline, Air France chairman Christian Blanc said on Monday in an interview in regional newspaper Le Provencal.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect AOM to run into positioning difficulties. We will certainly consider it, together with our shareholders. One must not forget that Brussels (European Commission) will allow Air France to buy another company from January 1, 1997,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Blanc said AOM -- which is up for sale by a state structure selling off Credit Lyonnais assets -- &quot;is a managed company, with an able staff, which has not entered a suicidal price cut race&quot; like insolvent competitor Air Liberte.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
